      body: "Dwellings of Eldervale is an epic-scale euro with an ameritrash heart. You lead one of eight asymmetric factions competing to settle a wild elemental world, placing workers to gather resources, summon monsters, cast spells and build dwellings — but here a worker can be forced out by combat, so placement and area control blur into one aggressive puzzle. It looks lavish, with oversized components and towering creatures, yet the engine underneath is a tight fight over elemental magic and board dominance. It scales from a solo challenge up to a full five-player table and rewards bold, adaptable play. A showpiece game for groups who want strategy with a big fantasy spectacle wrapped around it.",
