      body: "Calico looks adorable and plays like a genuinely tricky puzzle. You are sewing a quilt, drafting and placing hexagonal patch tiles to satisfy three demands at once: match colours to lure in picky cats, match patterns to earn buttons, and complete your quilt's design goals. The catch is that every tile can only sit in one spot, and pleasing the cats often fights against pleasing the buttons — so each placement is a satisfying little knot of competing priorities. It is a compact, colourful, surprisingly thinky game with an excellent solo mode and a warm, tactile table presence. Perfect for puzzle lovers and anyone who wants a small box that delivers a real strategic squeeze.",
